{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>The Rephaim were also counted as the Anakim.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, explained: You think that this is the land of the Rephaim that I gave to Abraham, because the Emim — who are Rephaim — formerly dwelt in it; but this is not it, for those Rephaim I dispossessed and gave them to the children of Lot, and settled others in their place. Those Emim were counted as Rephaim like the Anakim, who are called Rephaim, on account of that all who see them — their hands grow slack (נתרפות). Emim — on account of that their terror (אימתן) is cast upon creatures. And likewise: ובשעיר ישבו החורי — and in Seir the Horites dwelt — they are the children of Seir the Horite, and I gave it to the children of Esau."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:51.345008634Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}